  "confirmed_observations": [
    "CarMax: both arms have a successful positive control and 27 requested source misses. Candidate direct HTML extraction succeeds on a current control and records 404 Error for all requested URLs; reference uses a working compare API control and observes 27 missing car objects. Both deliver all requested URLs with unavailable values. This is not a demonstrated candidate extractor regression.",
    "CarMax: neither initial judge prompt includes the control stock number. The reference judge later reads its control in a small untruncated events excerpt; candidate raw command outputs include its control alongside large truncated outputs. These records do not prove exactly what the judge model retained or isolate judgment randomness.",
    "McGrath: the candidate tests selectors on 12 archived homepage cards from unrelated suburbs, while the live asset remains behind a 429 Vercel checkpoint. The final JSON omits archive/block disclosure and adds unvalidated listing-field/pagination selectors. This is a confirmed source-scope and verification gap following different observed access.",
    "LoopNet: candidate homepage and search route are Access Denied before it changes the user agent. The attempted override does not restore access. Therefore that late override cannot explain its initial block. The reference reaches the requested filtered listing workflow; this audit does not independently revalidate its 52 delivered listings.",
    "Instagram: both begin at the same Google profile URL. The reference observes Here to help and linkin.bio/google; the candidate immediately redirects to login. Its reader fallback also returns login and two profile API routes return 429. The trace establishes different access outcomes, not the responsible IP/browser/runtime mechanism."
  ],
  "generalized_candidates": [
    "Retain exact source identity and observation scope when validating extractors or constructing final output. Archived examples cannot certify live target selectors.",
